# Whole-germ restrictions of the finite semilinear common charts

The four finite charts carry one intrinsic selected-`B` germ anchor to the
normalized `e`, `a`, `b`, and genuine algebraic-output `c` maps in their
literal common finite target.  The declarations are split by chart so the
deeply dependent public types serialize with a bounded memory footprint.
